  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------- editorial text */
  prose: [
    { f: 'gut health, science', title: 'Why gut health comes first', paragraphs: ['Gut health is the foundation of whole-body wellness in dogs. When the gut is healthy, everything from digestion to immunity to mood works better. When it isn’t, issues stack up slowly and often silently.', 'So we clinically tested our food. Over 45 days, dogs that switched to Kismet showed measurable improvements in gut-health biomarkers.'], quote: 'Everything in the formula has a job to do.' },
    { f: 'ingredients, how we developed the food', title: 'How we developed our food for dogs', paragraphs: ['We prioritized the ingredients needed for a high-quality, nutritious recipe, without adding trendy ones that don’t add value. The formula is also defined by what’s not in it: no corn or wheat, no artificial flavors, colors or preservatives, and no animal by-product meals.', 'Everything we chose is included at the amount necessary to provide nutritional benefits. We did this even though it costs a little more.'], quote: 'The fruits and vegetables aren’t just pixie dust.' },
    { f: 'brand story, founders letter', title: 'Why we started Kismet', paragraphs: ['Dogs have always been a big part of our lives. But most dog brands never really spoke to us or felt true to what pet parenting is like. Dogs can be sweet, playful, silly, and also messy, unhinged and sometimes total trolls.', 'So we made something different: a brand for pets and their people, starting with premium dry food that’s every bit as nutritious as fresh, but way more convenient and affordable.'], quote: 'We’re excited you found us. It’s Kismet.' },
    { f: 'why dry food versus fresh', title: 'Why we chose dry over fresh', paragraphs: ['We felt strongly about using the safest, most proven method out there. With dry food, the process has been used for decades: we know how ingredients hold up and how long vitamins and minerals last.', 'Raw food has issues with microbial control, and fresh food has a higher chance of recall and needs a fridge. Neither is necessarily better nutritionally, and both cost a lot more.'], quote: 'Not all kibble is created equal.' },
    { f: 'new retailer or new store announcement', title: 'Kismet is closer than ever', paragraphs: ['We started online, but dogs don’t wait for shipping. Now you can pick up the same vet-developed recipes in person, on a trip you’re already making.', 'Same food, same guarantee, same very good dogs on the bag.'], quote: 'See you in the pet aisle.' },
    { f: 'cause, giving back', title: 'Make a purchase, help a pup', paragraphs: ['Every sale benefits a dog in need. Project Street Vet, founded by our Chief Vet Dr. Kwane Stewart, provides free veterinary care to the pets of people experiencing homelessness.', 'Paws for Life K9 Rescue sends dogs from overcrowded shelters to training programs that change lives on both ends of the leash.'], quote: 'The real stars here are dogs and the humans who love them.' },
  ],

